<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6913" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cărystŏs</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-us</span></b> , i, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάρυστος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A very ancient town on the south coast of
				Eubœa</i>, <i>famous for its
			marble</i>, now <i>Karysto</i> or <i>Castel Rosso</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 7, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				21, § 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
			17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tib. 3, 3, 14 al.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Derivv.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cărystēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Carystos</i>, <i>Carystian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vada,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 282</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 6, 11, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">16, 5, 15</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cărystĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 12, 21, § 64</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">36, 6, 7,
				§ 48</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columellae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 5, 6, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">LAPIDICINAE,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2964</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Căry-stĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Carystos</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 32,
				16, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town in Liguria</i>, now <i>Carosio</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 42, 7, 3</span></i>.</div>
